  "story": {
    "summary": "Stops the generator and analyzer from crashing when a `[MessagePackObject]` member is a closed generic struct from a referenced assembly. It does three things. Two `DeclaringSyntaxReferences[0]` lookups now tolerate a symbol that has no syntax. A new `PropertyDeclarationSyntax` lookup uses a safe `as` cast. Every diagnostic the TypeCollector reports now goes through a wrapper, which drops any diagnostic whose location is not a source tree in the current compilation. Three new tests compile a defining assembly to a metadata image and run the generator against a consumer of it. The change also turns off `EnforceCodeStyleInBuild` for the whole repo and adds README and MsgPack004 docs.",
    "why": "Issue #2283: diagnostic code in `GetObjectInfo` indexes `DeclaringSyntaxReferences[0]`. That collection is empty for metadata symbols, so the run throws `IndexOutOfRangeException`. As a result the generator emits no resolver at all.",
    "touches_beyond_requirement": [
      "Directory.Build.props switches EnforceCodeStyleInBuild from true to false for the whole repository.",
      "A global diagnostic filter (ReportIfLocatedInCompilation) silently drops any TypeCollector diagnostic whose location is Location.None or another tree. This applies to source types too, not only metadata types.",
      "README.md and doc/analyzers/MsgPack004.md gain new user-facing statements about how diagnostics behave for referenced types."
    ],
    "confidence_overview": "Medium that the reported repro no longer crashes; the tests reproduce it closely. Lower confidence that all crash sites are fixed. The issue names three indexing sites, the diff changes two, and the third (reported around line 735) does not appear in the diff. Low confidence that the global diagnostic filter does not hide legitimate diagnostics that previously had no location."
  },
